# UI and style rules

This project is an admin panel built with:

- Semantic HTML5.
- Modern JavaScript without a framework.
- Bootstrap 5.
- Custom CSS only when Bootstrap does not cover the requirement.

All new screens and visual changes must follow these rules.

## 1. Bootstrap 5

- Use Bootstrap 5 as the primary styling library.
- Do not use Bootstrap 4 (or older) classes.
- Do not add another CSS library that duplicates Bootstrap features.
- Prefer official Bootstrap components before creating custom ones.
- Use Bootstrap utilities for:
  - Spacing.
  - Colors.
  - Flexbox.
  - Grid.
  - Alignment.
  - Display.
  - Borders.
  - Shadows.
  - Typography.
  - Responsive design.
- Do not manually recreate styles Bootstrap already provides.
- Do not mix Bootstrap with ad-hoc or inconsistent styles.
- Interactive Bootstrap components must be initialized correctly via `bootstrap.bundle.min.js`.
- Always use Bootstrap Bundle when dropdowns, modals, tooltips, popovers, offcanvas, or collapse are needed.

If Bootstrap is not configured yet, integrate it centrally in the main layout.

Allowed example:

```html
<link
  href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
  rel="stylesheet"
>

<script
  src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"
></script>
```
